<v Ira Glass>（音乐 - The Cramps的“面具背后是什么”）

00:47:21.320 --> 00:47:36.640
<v Ira Glass>Act Three, The Unmasking. Well, now the story of masks that are not metaphorical, of guys who wear Lycra masks and brightly colored capes and wrestle for a living in Mexican wrestling matches known as lucha libre, which roughly translates to "free fight." RJ Smith tells the story.
<v Ira Glass>第三幕，“摘下面具”。现在是关于面具的故事，那些不是隐喻的面具，那些穿着莱卡面具和色彩鲜艳斗篷的家伙，他们在墨西哥摔跤比赛中以此为生，比赛被称为“墨西哥自由摔跤（lucha libre）”，大致翻译为“自由搏击”。RJ·史密斯讲述了这个故事。

00:47:36.640 --> 00:48:18.840
<v Rj Smith>Something about a mask makes a man brazen. That's the thing Atomic Blue taught me. Atomic Blue was the first Mexican wrestler I met. Picture a man in a skull-hugging blue mask, an atom drawn across the forehead, not to mention his Matt Helm black turtleneck, black jeans, tweed jacket, and really fine leather shoes. If Atomic Blue had a code ring, he'd be encrypting. If he had a martini, he'd be imbibing. He's bad. It's Atomic Blue who taught me that Mexican wrestling is not just a sport. Lucha libre is an art form, a tradition, a battle of good versus evil. Lucha libre, Atomic Blue said, is religion.
<v Rj Smith>面具里的某种东西让人变得胆大妄为。这就是原子蓝教会我的。原子蓝是我见过的第一个墨西哥摔跤手。想象一个戴着紧贴头颅的蓝色面具的男人，额头上画着一个原子，更不用说他那马特·赫尔姆风格的黑色高领毛衣、黑色牛仔裤、粗花呢夹克和非常精致的皮鞋。如果原子蓝有解码戒指，他会进行加密。如果他有马丁尼，他会啜饮。他很棒。是原子蓝教会我墨西哥摔跤不仅仅是一项运动。墨西哥自由摔跤是一种艺术形式，一种传统，一场正义对抗邪恶的战斗。原子蓝说，墨西哥自由摔跤是宗教。

00:48:18.840 --> 00:48:22.960
<v El Santo>[SPEAKING SPANISH].
<v El Santo>（西班牙语讲话）。

00:48:22.960 --> 00:48:52.580
<v Rj Smith>The greatest of all wrestling heroes was El Santo, "The Saint," who not only fought in the ring, but on the screen. From the '40s down to the present, dozens of wrestling stars have played in hundreds of incredibly strange movies, wrapping their limbs around plot devices pried from horror, crime, and science fiction genres. Santo might easily break up a spy ring, pitch woo at a backseat full of chicas, and defeat martians, all in the same picture.
<v Rj Smith>最伟大的摔跤英雄是“圣徒（El Santo）”，他不仅在擂台上战斗，也在银幕上战斗。从40年代到现在，几十位摔跤明星在数百部极其奇特的电影中扮演角色，将四肢缠绕在从恐怖、犯罪和科幻类型中强行剥离出来的剧情装置上。圣徒可以轻松捣毁一个间谍组织，在满是辣妹的后座上调情，并打败火星人，所有这些都在同一部电影里完成。

00:48:52.580 --> 00:49:00.850
<v El Santo>[SPEAKING SPANISH].
<v El Santo>（西班牙语讲话）。

00:49:00.850 --> 00:49:20.810
<v Rj Smith>Santo did everything without removing his disguise. Even when he directed his pictures, even when he was buried in 1984, Mexico's saint always kept his mask on.
<v Rj Smith>圣徒做一切事情都不摘下伪装。即使当他导演自己的电影时，即使在1984年他被埋葬时，墨西哥的圣徒总是戴着他的面具。

00:49:20.810 --> 00:49:57.640
<v Rj Smith>We're in a parking lot behind an Anaheim swap meet. Every weekend, they pull a plastic tarp off a regulation ring, set up metal bleachers. It's $10 for adults, who bring plenty of kids. About 50 fans surround the ring this afternoon. Shooting Star wears a black mask. Orange bolts crease his temples. In lucha libre, there are good guys, known as "tecnicos," and bad guys, "rudos." Guess which one Shooting Star is.
<v Rj Smith>我们在阿纳海姆一个跳蚤市场后面的停车场。每个周末，他们都会从一个标准的擂台上拉下一块塑料防水布，架起金属看台。成年人门票10美元，他们带来很多孩子。大约50名粉丝今天下午围在擂台周围。流星（Shooting Star）戴着黑色面具。橙色的螺栓弄皱了他的太阳穴。在墨西哥自由摔跤中，有被称作“技术流（tecnicos）”的好人，和“粗鲁派（rudos）”的坏人。猜猜流星是哪一种。

00:49:57.640 --> 00:50:00.500
<v Shooting Star>What country are you guys in, huh?
<v Shooting Star>你们这些家伙在哪个国家，嗯？

00:50:00.500 --> 00:50:03.840
<v Audience>USA! USA!
<v Audience>美国！美国！

00:50:03.840 --> 00:50:07.670
<v Audience>Mexico! Mexico! Mexico!
<v Audience>墨西哥！墨西哥！墨西哥！

00:50:07.670 --> 00:50:22.220
<v Rj Smith>Every time he yells, "USA," fans scream back, "Mexico!" Shooting Star preens before the hostile crowd. He issues challenges to his opponent, to the fans, and, it seems, maybe even to God. It's getting ugly.
<v Rj Smith>每次他大喊“美国”，粉丝们就尖叫着回应“墨西哥！”流星在敌对的人群面前显得十分傲慢。他向对手、向粉丝，甚至似乎向神发出挑战。情况变得糟糕了。

00:50:22.220 --> 00:50:25.990
<v Man>[SPEAKING SPANISH].
<v Man>（西班牙语讲话）。

00:50:25.990 --> 00:50:32.830
<v Shooting Star>I didn't quite get that, did you? I don't under-- English, maybe? Is English the country--
<v Shooting Star>我不完全明白那个，你明白吗？我不明白——英语，也许？英语是那个国家——

00:50:32.830 --> 00:50:56.620
<v Rj Smith>In Spanish, Shooting Star calls the hecklers "dirty wetbacks," asks if they're citizens of the US. It seems like everything in Mexican culture, people's worries and fears, plays out in the ring. So it's no surprise that there's a wrestler who's the equivalent of a masked Governor Pete Wilson playing the bad guy, taunting the immigrants in the crowd. What happens in Mexican life happens again in the ring.
<v Rj Smith>用西班牙语，流星称起哄者为“肮脏的背水者（墨西哥非法移民蔑称）”，询问他们是否是美国公民。似乎墨西哥文化中的一切，人们的担忧和恐惧，都在擂台上展现。所以有一个摔跤手相当于一个戴着面具的皮特·威尔逊州长，扮演坏人，嘲弄人群中的移民，这并不奇怪。墨西哥生活中发生的事情在擂台上重演。

00:50:56.620 --> 00:51:01.910
<v Shooting Star>No one's talking to you, so you just keep your mouth shut.
<v Shooting Star>没人跟你说话，所以你闭上你的嘴。

00:51:01.910 --> 00:51:24.950
<v Rj Smith>A couple years ago, when reports of a blood-sucking creature feasting on farm animals first shocked Mexico, a new wrestling star called The Goat Sucker suddenly appeared. Other heroes include wrestling priests and social workers. In today's match, one of the luchadores was named El Cholo, a wrestler dressed as a gang banger in saggy pants and colors, flashing gang signs.
<v Rj Smith>几年前，当关于一种以农场动物为食的吸血生物的报道首次震惊墨西哥时，一个名为“吸山羊怪”的新摔跤明星突然出现了。其他英雄包括摔跤牧师和社会工作者。在今天的比赛中，其中一名自由摔跤手名叫埃尔·乔洛（El Cholo），一个打扮成帮派成员的摔跤手，穿着松垮的裤子和帮派颜色，闪现帮派手势。

00:51:24.950 --> 00:52:07.530
<v Rj Smith>The luchadore reaches back to prehistoric mass religious rituals of American Indians and echoes to this moment. Many have pointed out how the suave, pipe-smoking, ski-masked, sub-commander Marcos, leader of the Zapatista rebels in northern Mexico, calculatedly evokes the image of El Santo. It's as if Hulk Hogan somehow carried within his form overtones of Daniel Boone and Martin Luther King.
<v Rj Smith>这位自由摔跤手回溯到美洲印第安人史前大众宗教仪式，并呼应着此时此刻。许多人指出，那在墨西哥北部领导萨帕塔叛军的斯文、抽烟斗、戴滑雪面具、副指挥官马科斯，是如何刻意唤起“圣徒”的形象。就好像绿巨人霍根以某种方式在他的形式中承载了丹尼尔·布恩和马丁·路德·金的弦外之音。

00:52:07.530 --> 00:52:28.710
<v Rj Smith>This is the power of the mask. It makes superheroes out of die cutters, mechanics, gardeners. In Anaheim, I even met a wrestler who was a chiropractic student. In the ring, a character named El Genie wears harem pants and performs a move he calls "the magic lamp." During the week, the tall, beefy man with a black pony tail is a car upholsterer.
<v Rj Smith>这就是面具的力量。它把模具切割工、机械师、园丁变成了超级英雄。在阿纳海姆，我甚至遇到了一位是脊椎按摩医学生的摔跤手。在擂台上，一个名为“精灵（El Genie）”的角色穿着灯笼裤，表演他称之为“魔灯”的招式。平日里，这个留着黑色马尾辫的高大、强壮的男人是一个汽车装潢师。

00:52:28.710 --> 00:53:09.920
<v El Genie>When I first started doing this, it was hard to get back to doing what I did, to be in upholstery. Because I would miss being out there, being the superstar. I'd miss it. But in our culture, in the Mexican culture, you get a lot of respect. For example, every time I go to Mexico and I go out-- let's say I go to a dance or something-- I get special treatment. They give me a table, and they treat me to drinks. And it's kind of funny because that's how people are.
<v El Genie>当我刚开始做这个时，很难回到我以前做的事情，去做装潢。因为我会怀念在外面的时光，怀念做超级英雄。我会怀念它。但在我们的文化中，在墨西哥文化中，你会得到很多尊重。例如，每次我去墨西哥，我出门——比如说我去跳舞之类的——我会得到特殊待遇。他们给我一张桌子，请我喝酒。这很有趣，因为人就是那样。

00:53:09.920 --> 00:53:37.450
<v El Genie>As soon as you put the mask on, you feel like a total different person. If you're a "heel," which is a bad guy, all of a sudden, you feel this urge to hurt, to inflict pain. And if you're a "face," a good guy, you feel like you've got to go and save the world. It's funny, and it happens.
<v El Genie>一旦你戴上面具，你就会感觉自己是一个完全不同的人。如果你是一个“坏蛋（heel）”，也就是坏人，突然间，你会感觉到伤害、造成痛苦的冲动。如果你是一个“好人（face）”，你会感觉必须走出去拯救世界。这很有趣，它确实会发生。

00:53:37.450 --> 00:54:25.320
<v El Genie>When someone takes your mask off in the ring, and they just take it off, it's like a humiliation. You get humiliated when someone takes your mask off. Whoever loses that match has to take off their mask and never wrestle with it again. It happened to me, yeah. I went against one of the top wrestlers in Mexico. And I lost it in the Mexicali against Fishman. His name was Fishman. And he was my idol as I was growing up. But it came to a head. We had a rivalry that came to a head. And we bet our masks, and he got the better part. And that's the biggest humiliation you can receive in the ring, losing your mask.
<v El Genie>当有人在擂台上摘下你的面具时，他们就只是把它摘下来，这就像是一种羞辱。当有人摘下你的面具时，你会被羞辱。无论谁输了那场比赛，都必须摘下面具，永远不能再戴着它摔跤。它确实发生在我身上。我对抗了墨西哥顶级摔跤手之一。我在墨西卡利输给了“鱼人（Fishman）”。他的名字叫鱼人。他是我成长过程中的偶像。但它达到了顶点。我们有一场竞争达到了顶点。我们押上了我们的面具，他赢了。那是你在擂台上能受到的最大的羞辱，失去你的面具。

00:54:25.320 --> 00:55:14.380
<v Rj Smith>I saw it once, and I'll never forget. It happened last spring. And for weeks after, I had dreams of masked men, wrestlers, hockey goalies, the guys in KISS. It was the last match of the night, Bulldog Rivera versus Shamu Junior. Shamu was a pudgy tecnico. Nobody had to wonder how he got the name Shamu, no wonder about the whale appliques decorating his Aqua Velva blue mask. The fight was even for a while. But then Bulldog climbs the ropes, leaps at Shamu Junior's torso, and knocks him to his knees. Shamu Junior's in a fog. And Bulldog smoothly reaches back for the laces binding his mask.
<v Rj Smith>我见过一次，我永远不会忘记。它发生在去年春天。之后几周，我梦见戴面具的人、摔跤手、冰球守门员、KISS乐队的人。那是当晚最后一场比赛，斗牛犬里维拉（Bulldog Rivera）对阵沙姆小弟（Shamu Junior）。沙姆是一个圆滚滚的“技术流”。没人需要怀疑他是怎么得到沙姆这个名字的，也无需怀疑那些装饰在他阿夸维尔瓦蓝色面具上的鲸鱼贴花。比赛势均力敌了一段时间。但随后斗牛犬爬上绳索，扑向沙姆小弟的躯干，把他撞倒在地。沙姆小弟在迷糊中。斗牛犬顺滑地伸手去够系住他面具的鞋带。

00:55:14.380 --> 00:56:02.820
<v El Genie>Oh, god. Everything was going through my-- I thought I would never do it again, I would never wrestle again, that people were just going to forget me right away because I had lost. And I wasn't going to get over it. And it felt-- I cried on top of the ring. I cried when I lost my mask. It was something-- god, it's hard to describe. But it was a feeling of-- I felt alone. I felt so alone that day. But that night, one of my sons was there. And he came up to the ring, and he gave me a hug. And it felt good. It felt a lot better. This is his words. He said, "You know, Dad, it's just a mask. You know?"
<v El Genie>哦，天哪。一切都在我的脑海中闪过——我以为我永远不会再做了，我永远不会再摔跤了，人们会因为我输了而立刻忘记我。我不会走出来。它感觉——我在擂台上哭了。我输掉面具时哭了。那是某种——天哪，很难描述。但那是一种——我感到孤独。那天我感到非常孤独。但那天晚上，我的一个儿子在那里。他走到擂台边，给了我一个拥抱。那感觉很好。感觉好多了。这是他的原话。他说：“你知道，爸爸，那只是个面具。你懂吗？”

00:56:02.820 --> 00:56:39.470
<v Rj Smith>The unmasking. It's the most sacramental moment. And over the next few minutes, Bulldog returns to the act at will, almost tenderly unlacing as Shamu Junior futilely resists. His head cradled in Bulldog's lap, Shamu Junior pleads with the ref. But then, Bulldog sends the ref sprawling with a kick. There is no hope now. Armed security men are restraining a lady in her 40s with a dye job. All around, there's a call for blood.
<v Rj Smith>摘下面具。这是最庄严的时刻。在接下来的几分钟里，斗牛犬随意地完成了动作，几乎温柔地解开，而沙姆小弟徒劳地反抗。沙姆小弟的头被抱着斗牛犬的怀里，恳求裁判。但随后，斗牛犬一脚把裁判踢开。现在没有希望了。武装警卫正在制止一位染了发的40多岁女士。周围到处都是对鲜血的呼唤。

00:56:39.470 --> 00:57:26.260
<v Rj Smith>In an act of lyric defiance, Shamu Junior undoes the rest of his own laces and flings his mask at his opponent. He is utterly humiliated. Losing your mask is like losing your ego, manhood, superpowers, and, since fans typically turn on you, your opportunity to make cash off the books. He buries his face in his hands, fighting off Bulldog's probing fingers. Finally, Bulldog pries away Shamu's hands, and we see his face. Degraded without the mask, he's just a guy, a buzz cut of dark hair, short on the sides. It's the day before Easter. Christ may have risen, but Shamu Junior is taking a fall.
<v Rj Smith>在一场抒情的反抗中，沙姆小弟解开了自己剩下的鞋带，并把面具扔向他的对手。他被彻底羞辱了。失去面具就像失去你的自尊、男子气概、超级能力，而且，因为粉丝通常会背叛你，你失去在书本之外赚钱的机会。他双手捂住脸，对抗着斗牛犬试探性的手指。最后，斗牛犬拨开沙姆的手，我们看到了他的脸。没有面具的贬低，他只是个家伙，留着黑发平头，侧面剪得很短。那是复活节前一天。基督可能复活了，但沙姆小弟正在倒下。

00:57:26.260 --> 00:57:30.610
<v Ira Glass>RJ Smith is a senior writer for Spin magazine. He had help in the field from Mandalit del Barco.
<v Ira Glass>RJ·史密斯是《Spin》杂志的资深作家。他在现场得到了曼达利特·德尔·巴尔科的帮助。

00:57:30.610 --> 00:57:36.850
